review:
Groundbreaking turn based isometric RPG set in a bleak retro futuristic post apocalyptic setting. Most of the gameplay and storytelling aged well, but people who expect fast paced action and easy progression are gonna be disappointed. Game can be easily run on a modern machine without any hustle (just turn X2 scaling in option). It is not for everybody, but this game is absolut classic, and it is a must play for every RPG lover.

Pros:
- Great atmosphere;
- Sense of urgency;
- Amazing eerie soundtrack;
- A lot of interesting characters;
- Cool art style;
- Awesome voice acting;
- Interesting lore;
- Gory combat;
- A lot of options in quests;
- Sense of mortality;
- Diverse SPECIAL system;
- Dark humor;
- Interesting and mature story;

Cons:
- Combat can get repetitive;
- Very steep difficulty curve;
- Some quests solutions are very obscure;
- A lot of pixel hunting;
- Companions CONSTANTLY block your movement;
